# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout commits CRLF, the Linux CI runner sees every
# line of every file as changed, and diffs between the two bench machines are
# unreadable. `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repo AND checks out LF, so
# every machine and the CI runner agree byte-for-byte.
#
# After adding this file once, run:  git add --renormalize .
* text=auto eol=lf

# Firmware and binary artifacts must never be line-ending mangled.
*.bin  binary
*.elf  binary
*.hex  binary
*.a    binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
